.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH baby 1  "baby 0.10.6" 
.SH NAME
baby \- Build a project from a recipe and install its binary
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbaby\fR [\fB\-\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-strip\fR] [\fB\-\-backup\fR] [\fB\-\-service\fR] [\fB\-\-sudo\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-clean\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-boar\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-lock\fR] [\fB\-\-lock\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-lock\-lease\fR] [\fB\-\-repo\-lock\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-target\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-install\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-recipe\fR] [\fB\-\-check\-recipe\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIRUN_ARGS\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
BABY — Build And Bin Yield
.PP
Build a project from a validated installation recipe and install its binary.
.PP
By default the binary is installed to /usr/local/bin. Use \-\-user to install
to ~/.local/bin instead, or \-\-install\-dir for a custom location.
.PP
Examples:
  baby                      # build + install to /usr/local/bin
  baby \-\-user               # build + install to ~/.local/bin
  baby \-\-run                # build + install + execute
  baby \-\-run \-\- \-\-help      # pass \-\-help to the installed binary
  baby \-\-dry\-run            # preview what would be done
  baby \-\-recipe .baby.toml  # use an explicit versioned installation recipe
  baby update               # check for updates (\-\-stable by default)
  baby update \-\-nightly     # check for nightly builds
  baby update \-\-bleeding    # check for bleeding edge builds
  baby boom                 # discover and update all managed tools
  baby boom \-\-interactive   # select which tools to update interactively
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-run\fR
Build, install, then execute the binary
.TP
\fB\-\-strip\fR
Strip symbols before installing
.TP
\fB\-\-backup\fR
Backup existing binary before overwriting
.TP
\fB\-\-service\fR
Restart matching systemd service after install
.TP
\fB\-\-sudo\fR
Force privileged (sudo) install
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR
Install to ~/.local/bin instead of /usr/local/bin
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would happen without executing
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-clean\fR
Keep build artefacts after installation
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-boar\fR
Never delegate a failed build to `boar` for RAM/disk recovery
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-lock\fR
Skip all locksmithd coordination (repo\-wide wait and project lease)
.TP
\fB\-\-lock\-timeout\fR \fI<SECS>\fR
Seconds to wait for a contended locksmith lease (default: 300)
.TP
\fB\-\-lock\-lease\fR \fI<SECS>\fR
Seconds to request for the locksmith lease duration (default: 1200)
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\-lock\-timeout\fR \fI<SECS>\fR
Seconds to wait for all repo\-wide locksmith leases to clear (default: 300)
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-dir\fR \fI<TARGET_DIR>\fR
Custom target directory (default: target/release)
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-dir\fR \fI<INSTALL_DIR>\fR
Custom install directory (overrides \-\-user)
.TP
\fB\-\-recipe\fR \fI<RECIPE>\fR
Versioned installation recipe (default: .baby.toml, then Cargo.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-check\-recipe\fR
Validate and print the resolved recipe without executing it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIRUN_ARGS\fR]
Pass additional arguments when running with \-\-run
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBbaby update\fR [\fB\-\-stable\fR|\fB\-\-nightly\fR|\fB\-\-bleeding\fR]
Check for available updates. Exactly one channel may be given;
\-\-stable is the default.
.TP
\fBbaby boom\fR [\fB\-\-init\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-parallelism\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\fR \fILIST\fR]
Discover and update all managed tools in parallel. \-\-init writes a new
.boom.toml instead of updating. \-\-filter takes a comma\-separated list of
tool names.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success: the project was built and installed (or the requested check,
update, or boom run completed without errors).
.TP
1
Failure: recipe validation, build, install, lock acquisition, or the
command run failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .baby.toml
Versioned installation recipe in the project root (preferred).
.TP
.I Cargo.toml
Fallback recipe source when no .baby.toml exists.
.TP
.I .boom.toml
Managed-tools list used by \fBbaby boom\fR (\-\-init creates it).
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin
Default installation directory (override with \-\-user or \-\-install\-dir).
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin
Per\-user installation directory (used with \-\-user).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR birthctl (1),
.BR birthd (1),
.BR boar (1)
.SH VERSION
v0.10.6
